        ":question/id": "f618a7fb-c5a6-5658-a8d2-b99235d841c5",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-113948",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int -\\frac{5}{2}{csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cot}x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{5}{2}{csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}(-\\operatorname{cot}x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      {
        ":db/id": 17592186233200,
        ":knowledge-point/_questions": [
          {
            ":knowledge-point/id": "9836abbe-e172-5c2f-8b19-145ef6d5c02d",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Integrating Cosecant Squared"
